{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>On the day he gives as an inheritance</b> — in the time to come. He may not give firstborn status — \"for they are My firstborn sons, Israel.\"" "<b>On the day he gives as an inheritance to his sons</b> — ס\"ת מותו. As for what Rabbi Yehudah said: three who entered to visit the sick — by day, they may write [a bill] or they may render judgment; by night, they may write but may not render judgment — and this is what he commands at the time of death: if it is by day, it has the status of Torah law." "<b>את אשר יהיה ל</b>ו. In gematria — teaches that the son takes from the expected as from the held." "<b>את אשר יהיה לו</b> — ס\"ת תורה. That he may not give an inheritance to one who transgresses the words of Torah. And if he gave to another in language of inheritance, it is nothing, because he stipulated against what is written in the Torah, and anyone who stipulates against what is written in the Torah — his words are nothing."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {1 "ס\"ת מותו = the stum/sotert (first and last letters of consecutive words) spell מות, 'death.' His Aramaic-style למאי דא\"ר ('as for what R. Yehudah said') rendered literally.", 3 "ס\"ת תורה = the stum/sotert (first and last letters of the phrase) spell תורה, 'Torah.'"}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:10:15.109372429Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}